  "contentHtml": "\n    \n    \n        \n                <ul>\n                    \n                     <li><a href=\"/news/diagnostics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Diagnostics</a></li>                     <li>1 min read</li>                 </ul>\n                            \n        \n                                    \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/12345678/Reuters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Reuters</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Oct 22, 2026 at 03:54 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Bengaluru: Molecular testing company <a href=\"/tag/qiagen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Qiagen</a> said on Wednesday Swedish buyout firm <a href=\"/tag/eqt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">EQT</a> would acquire it for about €9.6 billion ($10.78 billion).EQT offered €46.50 ($52.22) a share for Qiagen, representing an 8.6% premium to its last close.The buyout ends years of takeover speculation surrounding the European <a href=\"/tag/diagnostics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">diagnostics</a> firm and reflects increasing private-equity appetite in the sector, where growing demand for molecular testing has made companies attractive acquisition targets.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                    \n\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/12345678/Reuters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Reuters</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 22, 2026 at 03:54 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 22, 2026 at 03:54 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n             